# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# Neither of these is a secret. They identify an Azure app registration and a
# tenant; this app uses a public-client device-code flow and has no client secret
# at all. They live here rather than in config.py only so the same code can run
# against a different tenant unchanged.
#
# To obtain them: Azure Portal -> Microsoft Entra ID -> App registrations ->
# New registration. Choose "Accounts in this organizational directory only" and
# no redirect URI. Under Authentication, enable "Allow public client flows".
# Under API permissions add the delegated scopes Files.Read.All, Sites.Read.All
# and User.Read.
#
# Note: those are read scopes. They typically still require an admin to grant
# consent on first use, but that is a much smaller ask than the write scopes the
# original design needed -- an admin is approving a tool that provably cannot
# alter anything.

MOVEIN_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
MOVEIN_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
